commodore-900-coh-kernel3
==========================

COHERENT 3.x kernel sources for the Zilog Z8001-based Commodore 900. This
repository contains the portable kernel, Z8001 machine layer, console drivers,
kernel headers, and host-side build tools.

`kernel3` describes the source lineage. It is separate from the older
0.7-derived kernel.

Building
--------

    make deps                 fetch the toolchain and kboot inputs
    make                      build the kernel
    make drivers              build the loadable console and hostfs drivers
    make kernel-dist          create the kernel package
    make kernel-headers-dist  create the standalone headers package
    make check-stamps         verify kernel/driver link IDs
    make clean
    make help

The kernel is written to `os/hostbuild/kobj/kernel.out`. Set
`C900_TOOLCHAIN` or `C900_KBOOT` to use local checkouts instead of the inputs
selected by `DEPS`.

The compiler that produced a kernel is recorded in
`os/hostbuild/kobj/kernel.stamp` and reported by `make check-stamps`. `DEPS`
takes the toolchain's latest release; `make deps DEP=toolchain` fetches it.

The kernel must be booted by kboot: it is larger than the ROM loader can read.

This repository builds kernel artifacts only. Disk images and userland are
built in their respective repositories.

Hardware
--------

The boot picks a console driver for the display card it finds:

- LR (lo-res) card: `lrtty`, plus its four serial lines as tty52-55.
- HR card, 1024x800 or 1024x1024 mono: `hrtty`.
- HR card in colour, 640x400: `hrctty`.
- LC card (8563): `lctty`, with bitmap graphics on `/dev/lcvdc`.
- No card: the serial console (`notty`).

Two hard disks
--------------

The kernel drives a second hard disk of a different geometry, with limits:

- Drive 1's geometry must be patched into `/coherent` at the symbol
  `wdparam1_`: 6 bytes `0f`, `heads<<4 | cyl>>8`, `cyl & ff`, `precomp/16`,
  `rwc/16`, `sectors`. Left zero, drive 1 is taken to match drive 0.
- Drive 1 uses drive 0's partition table, so its partitions must fit drive 1.
- No `/dev` nodes for drive 1 are shipped. Its minor is 0x10 + partition:

      /etc/mknod /dev/hd17 b 2 17; /etc/mknod /dev/rhd17 c 2 17

- Each switch between drives costs one extra controller command.

